// Truth sources for the ecommerce golden set.
//
// Deliberately semantics-free: raw columns, no measures, no docs, no joins, no
// filters. A truthQuery that reused ecommerce.malloy's `total_sales` would let a
// bug in the semantic model certify its own golden, which is the one thing this
// file exists to prevent.
//
// It lives in the package (rather than the query text) because the Publisher's
// query endpoint rejects `duckdb.table(...)` in a restricted query. Inside a
// model file the same reference is allowed, so goldens run through the
// Publisher's API like everything else.
//
// Table paths resolve from the PACKAGE ROOT, so they are written
// 'data/x.parquet'. A sibling-relative '../data/x.parquet' compiles and then
// fails at read time. `data` here is a symlink to ../ecommerce/data: this
// package is a second lens on the same 20MB, not a copy of it.
//
// This is a SEPARATE package from `ecommerce` on purpose. It used to live at
// ecommerce/gold/truth.malloy, inside the tree the Publisher serves, where its
// raw sources were indexed next to the semantic model and could come back from
// get_context -- quietly changing what the model under test looked like.

source: order_items is duckdb.table('data/order_items.parquet')

source: users is duckdb.table('data/users.parquet')

source: products is duckdb.table('data/products.parquet')

source: inventory_items is duckdb.table('data/inventory_items.parquet')
